WEBVTT

00:07.296 --> 00:09.715
[children playing]

00:11.675 --> 00:13.510
[laughing]

00:16.138 --> 00:18.432
Tarao! Want a tomato?

00:18.515 --> 00:19.767
-Thank you.
-Mmm.

00:19.850 --> 00:21.185
-[pencil scratching]
-[children laughing]

00:21.268 --> 00:23.270
[children chattering]

00:31.570 --> 00:32.571
Mimihime.

00:34.198 --> 00:35.866
What are you daydreaming for?

00:36.367 --> 00:37.660
Class is about to start.

00:38.202 --> 00:39.203
Oh.

00:40.621 --> 00:42.331
We have a test today.

00:42.414 --> 00:45.000
What? Today's just a normal class, right?

00:45.084 --> 00:46.669
But, we do have one.

00:47.294 --> 00:48.796
<i>Get ready for the test.</i>

00:48.879 --> 00:50.839
-[all] Huh?
-You never said.

00:51.423 --> 00:54.260
Teacher! I haven't studied at all.
It's impossible.

00:54.343 --> 00:56.971
Even if you had, it'd be impossible.

00:57.054 --> 00:58.305
-What?
-[student chuckles]

00:58.389 --> 01:00.099
[robot teacher] <i>Everyone, please be quiet.</i>

01:00.683 --> 01:02.893
<i>If you paid attention in class,
you'll be fine.</i>

01:04.603 --> 01:06.397
-<i>There are ten questions.
</i>-[student 2] Hmm…

01:11.193 --> 01:13.696
Why does the fish have arms?

01:13.779 --> 01:17.616
Well, to catch other fish of course.

01:17.700 --> 01:18.951
Have you seen one before?

01:19.451 --> 01:21.370
No, I just made it up!

01:21.453 --> 01:22.705
Okay.

01:23.747 --> 01:24.999
It's weird.

01:25.082 --> 01:26.083
Strange, right?

01:26.667 --> 01:30.254
Yeah, but I want to show the Director.
It's funny!

01:30.879 --> 01:32.172
Can I have it?

01:32.673 --> 01:34.675
-When I've finished it, okay?
-Okay.

01:35.592 --> 01:37.386
[robot teacher] <i>Fifteen minutes left.</i>

01:37.469 --> 01:39.680
Geez! Come on.

01:41.015 --> 01:43.142
-[electronic shutdown]
-Hmm.

01:45.894 --> 01:50.065
DO YOU WANT TO GO OUTSIDE
OF THE OUTSIDE?

01:52.609 --> 01:54.028
Outside of…

01:54.695 --> 01:55.779
the outside?

01:55.863 --> 01:57.448
[rocks scattering]

02:06.623 --> 02:13.630
TENGOKU-DAIMAKYO

02:16.383 --> 02:17.843
[crows cawing]

02:27.394 --> 02:30.064
So, shall we go hunting for treasure?

02:30.647 --> 02:32.775
Sure, okay.

02:33.525 --> 02:35.527
This neighborhood
doesn't seem too messed up.

02:35.611 --> 02:38.572
We need to find houses
that haven't been broken into.

02:38.655 --> 02:40.407
Let's go further in then.

02:42.326 --> 02:45.245
[scavenger] It's locked.
That's a good sign.

02:45.829 --> 02:49.625
Wait, Maru? Where are you? Hey, Maru!

02:49.708 --> 02:52.961
Sis! We can get in from over here!

02:53.879 --> 02:56.256
The windows are barely broken.

02:56.340 --> 02:57.883
I guess no one's been in here yet.

03:02.930 --> 03:04.807
Oh, it's a total wreck.

03:06.600 --> 03:08.435
I'll go and check the other rooms.

03:08.519 --> 03:10.145
[Maru grunts]

03:11.230 --> 03:13.732
Oh, got a toothbrush.

03:14.233 --> 03:15.442
[Maru shouts] Sis!

03:15.526 --> 03:17.820
-[rustling]
-I found an unopened pack of toilet paper!

03:17.903 --> 03:20.823
Nice one. I'm dying!

03:22.741 --> 03:23.742
Oh, no!

03:24.785 --> 03:26.161
[grunts]

03:26.829 --> 03:31.333
Aah! Having a toilet makes all
the difference, even if it doesn't work.

03:31.917 --> 03:33.544
Hey, don't look!

03:33.627 --> 03:35.045
Well, shut the door then.

03:35.629 --> 03:37.047
There is no door.

03:37.131 --> 03:38.549
[Maru sighs]

03:38.632 --> 03:40.717
[stairs creak]

03:41.301 --> 03:44.263
As if, the roof is wide open.

03:44.847 --> 03:46.723
That's why this place is a dump.

03:47.433 --> 03:49.101
[Maru] I'm so hungry.

03:49.184 --> 03:50.686
[Sis] Don't say it.

03:50.769 --> 03:53.439
-[door opens]
-I'm trying not to think about it.

03:53.522 --> 03:54.606
Oh…

03:55.399 --> 03:56.400
What is it--

04:06.201 --> 04:10.789
[Sis] <i>Most of the people who survived
ended up dying of starvation.</i>

04:11.707 --> 04:13.584
<i>Since they died in this house,</i>

04:14.501 --> 04:16.378
<i>it means there's no food here.</i>

04:17.588 --> 04:19.173
Let's go to the next house.

04:19.756 --> 04:20.757
[Maru] Okay.

04:24.678 --> 04:27.598
Sis, this house is amazing.

04:28.182 --> 04:30.058
It's so glamorous.

04:30.142 --> 04:32.519
[Sis] Yeah, the people who lived here
must have been super rich.

04:32.603 --> 04:33.604
NAESHIRO FAMILY

04:33.687 --> 04:36.940
Wow, you finally opened the canned food?

04:37.524 --> 04:40.110
Well, we didn't exactly
find anything to eat, did we?

04:40.944 --> 04:43.780
Maru, can you find us
some plates or something?

04:43.864 --> 04:46.492
On it. I'm starved.

04:48.160 --> 04:51.371
Hey, what's this veg stuff?

04:51.955 --> 04:55.292
The weeds growing all over the place
around here. I think they're edible.

04:55.876 --> 04:58.045
I thought it might fill us up a bit more.

04:58.754 --> 04:59.880
Ooh.

05:01.089 --> 05:02.424
[crunch]

05:02.508 --> 05:04.426
[gasps, splutters]

05:04.510 --> 05:07.304
-[Maru] It's so bitter.
-[Sis] Spit it out!

05:07.387 --> 05:09.181
[coughing, gagging]

05:09.264 --> 05:12.643
It stunk out the whole dish.

05:12.726 --> 05:13.852
I'm sorry!

05:13.936 --> 05:16.188
That was our precious canned food!

05:16.271 --> 05:18.315
[Sis] I said I'm sorry!

05:19.274 --> 05:21.944
[raindrops pattering]

05:32.371 --> 05:34.665
Is that your boyfriend?

05:35.249 --> 05:36.333
You're awake?

05:36.833 --> 05:38.627
[Maru] I can never fall asleep.

05:39.127 --> 05:41.421
You're always fast asleep way before me.

05:41.505 --> 05:45.342
Really?
I guess I'm a useless bodyguard then.

05:46.051 --> 05:48.220
I'm fine protecting myself.

05:48.887 --> 05:50.264
You can go back if you want.

05:52.349 --> 05:56.186
One is my friend, and the other
is someone I want to see.

05:57.437 --> 06:00.440
If I can find them
while I take you to your destination,

06:00.524 --> 06:02.276
that'll be two birds with one stone.

06:02.985 --> 06:05.279
That's why it's important
I tag along with you.

06:05.904 --> 06:08.991
Anyway, I'm not gonna go anywhere
while you're sleeping,

06:09.491 --> 06:10.617
so you can relax.

06:15.330 --> 06:17.791
[thunderclap]

06:17.874 --> 06:19.167
[wind whistling]

06:21.211 --> 06:22.629
[crow screeches]

06:27.342 --> 06:29.970
HASSOU INN

06:39.646 --> 06:40.814
[footsteps approaching]

06:40.897 --> 06:43.692
[Sis] So, where shall we go today?

06:44.192 --> 06:47.070
[Maru] We don't have enough info to go on.

06:47.571 --> 06:49.281
I'm sick of wandering around aimlessly.

06:49.364 --> 06:52.367
[Sis chuckles]
Well then, let's start looking for others.

06:52.868 --> 06:54.494
Let's go somewhere that might be busy.

06:55.120 --> 06:57.914
[Maru] A place where people gather,

06:57.998 --> 07:01.877
like somewhere with land,
or near a station.

07:01.960 --> 07:03.587
Yeah, somewhere like that.

07:04.588 --> 07:07.924
For now,
let's walk alongside this railway track.

07:08.425 --> 07:10.802
Great! And I want a new pair of shoes.

07:11.386 --> 07:13.930
Okay, okay.
Let's keep an eye out for a store.

07:14.014 --> 07:16.767
[Maru] And after that,
I'm desperate for some tasty food!

07:17.851 --> 07:20.646
Are you still annoyed at me
for yesterday, or what?

07:20.729 --> 07:21.897
Huh?

07:21.980 --> 07:25.233
That's not what I meant!

07:25.776 --> 07:27.277
Guys like you

07:27.361 --> 07:30.906
are always saying stupid stuff like that,
even if it is by mistake.

07:31.865 --> 07:33.116
[gulps]

07:33.200 --> 07:34.284
[thug sniggering]

07:35.035 --> 07:36.161
[grunts]

07:36.745 --> 07:37.913
Women!

07:37.996 --> 07:40.332
Just when I thought life
wasn't worth living.

07:40.415 --> 07:41.625
Two women appear.

07:42.709 --> 07:44.002
I'm a man.

07:44.086 --> 07:46.880
[smacks lips, sighs]
Great, a little brat boy.

07:46.963 --> 07:48.465
I'm a boy too.

07:48.548 --> 07:49.633
I'm not stupid!

07:49.716 --> 07:53.178
All right, put down your heavy bags.

07:53.261 --> 07:55.263
I'm gonna take you to heaven.

07:56.098 --> 07:57.265
-[Sis sighs]
-[bag thuds]

07:57.349 --> 07:59.393
Just when I thought we'd found someone…

07:59.476 --> 08:01.019
-[hammer cocks]
-…it's just a couple of bums.

08:01.103 --> 08:02.020
[gasps]

08:02.104 --> 08:04.690
Whoa, wait. We don't have many bullets.
Don't waste them.

08:05.190 --> 08:07.859
Get outta here if you want to live!

08:07.943 --> 08:10.821
So our lives are worth less than bullets.

08:10.904 --> 08:15.575
They're from the lawless generation, whose
world ended before it had even begun.

08:15.659 --> 08:18.537
Who knows what they're capable of.
Let's go.

08:19.329 --> 08:22.165
Not like you could hit us anyway, fools!

08:22.249 --> 08:23.291
Damn.

08:23.875 --> 08:24.918
Hmm.

08:25.502 --> 08:27.713
Wait a sec. Is that even a real gun?

08:28.380 --> 08:29.381
[sighs]

08:31.466 --> 08:34.594
What's this, what's this?
Dropping it now, are we?

08:34.678 --> 08:37.639
-I've never seen a gun that weird before.
-[weapons clink]

08:37.723 --> 08:40.016
You're just bluffing
with some kid's plaything.

08:41.560 --> 08:42.561
[scoffs]

08:43.353 --> 08:44.521
Run!

08:45.522 --> 08:48.817
There's no escape!
I won't let you make us look like idiots!

08:48.900 --> 08:49.901
[grunts]

08:50.444 --> 08:52.571
-[knife swooshes]
-[grunting]

08:52.654 --> 08:53.530
[shouts]

08:54.448 --> 08:56.408
-[grunts]
-[weapon clatters]

09:00.787 --> 09:03.123
-[Maru grunts]
-[thug groans]

09:14.134 --> 09:16.344
-It shoots…
-[creaking]

09:16.428 --> 09:17.888
[all screaming]

09:20.474 --> 09:22.100
[groaning]

09:23.852 --> 09:28.273
So, you were saying something
about taking me to heaven?

09:28.356 --> 09:30.025
That was, I--

09:30.108 --> 09:31.860
-[hammer cocks]
-[whimpers]

09:31.943 --> 09:34.112
We're looking for it. Heaven.

09:34.863 --> 09:35.864
Take us there.

09:36.990 --> 09:37.991
MORIYAMA HOSPITAL

09:38.074 --> 09:41.661
Wow, what a flashy home you guys have.

09:42.329 --> 09:45.123
What do you think, Maru?
Anything catch your attention?

09:45.665 --> 09:48.168
No, nothing.

09:48.668 --> 09:50.003
[Sis] Right?

09:50.086 --> 09:52.506
There's no way this is the goal.
It'd be a miracle.

09:53.340 --> 09:56.927
Oh, there's a generator!
That's a generator, right?

09:57.761 --> 09:59.429
Can you charge my battery?

09:59.513 --> 10:02.015
Why would I do that? [whimpers]

10:02.098 --> 10:05.185
I don't think you're really grasping
the full reality of your situation.

10:05.685 --> 10:09.022
You attacked us,
but we turned the tables on you.

10:09.606 --> 10:12.567
Even if I decide to kill you,
you don't have the right to complain.

10:14.486 --> 10:17.280
We'll leave once the battery is full.

10:18.114 --> 10:19.115
Please.

10:19.199 --> 10:20.450
[groans]

10:22.702 --> 10:23.787
[groans]

10:24.871 --> 10:29.417
And while we're at it, you guys
heard of a place called "Heaven"?

10:30.043 --> 10:32.170
At this point, anywhere
with "heaven" in its name,

10:32.254 --> 10:35.298
or even a place you think
feels "just like heaven" will do.

10:35.382 --> 10:39.386
As if anything like heaven exists
since the Collapse.

10:39.469 --> 10:41.805
I understand that.

10:41.888 --> 10:44.099
That's why I tried to
make the question simpler for you.

10:44.182 --> 10:47.018
Do you guys like tomatoes?

10:47.102 --> 10:48.687
Ah, they're back.

10:49.187 --> 10:50.939
Why? Gonna give us some?

10:51.731 --> 10:56.611
If you do, then I've heard of something
you might call "heaven."

10:57.195 --> 10:59.698
-Maru, don't you like tomatoes?
-Love them.

11:00.448 --> 11:01.783
Tell us the details.

11:05.287 --> 11:06.580
Here.

11:06.663 --> 11:09.040
Oh, thank you so much!

11:09.624 --> 11:11.668
What kind of battery is that exactly?

11:13.712 --> 11:14.713
My gun battery.

11:14.796 --> 11:16.506
You little brat!

11:17.007 --> 11:20.677
You've been controlling us with a gun
that doesn't work this whole time.

11:20.760 --> 11:25.181
I wasn't even sure that last shot
was gonna fire. I was out of bullets.

11:25.265 --> 11:27.642
-[thugs groan]
-Right, Maru?

11:27.726 --> 11:31.104
Morons! I hope you die by the roadside.
Lawless youths!

11:31.187 --> 11:32.647
You should respect your elders!

11:32.731 --> 11:33.899
[thugs whimper, shout]

11:35.859 --> 11:38.194
[laughing]

11:40.405 --> 11:42.282
Phew, that was close.

11:42.365 --> 11:45.285
It was no big deal.
Just a bunch of old idiots.

11:46.119 --> 11:47.954
We got this charged up too!

11:48.038 --> 11:50.832
I feel so much better
now we've got four shots.

11:50.916 --> 11:53.877
It's probably better not to
count it as four shots.

11:53.960 --> 11:55.962
The number of times
that thing doesn't work…

11:57.172 --> 11:59.633
Well anyway, off to "Tomato Heaven."

12:01.301 --> 12:02.302
[both laugh]

12:02.886 --> 12:04.429
<i>What the hell is "Tomato Heaven"?</i>

12:06.473 --> 12:09.559
[student] I'm not really sure
that's the best way to hold an exam.

12:10.268 --> 12:13.605
Mimihime, how did you know there
was going to be a test?

12:13.688 --> 12:16.942
I don't know. I just had a hunch somehow.

12:18.151 --> 12:20.445
But there is one thing that is certain.

12:22.864 --> 12:27.702
Just because you know there's a test,
there's no promise of full marks.

12:27.786 --> 12:28.954
Ugh.

12:29.621 --> 12:33.375
Class is done! Let's play some sport.

12:34.167 --> 12:36.878
I want to continue working on this, so…

12:38.129 --> 12:39.339
Then, Anzu?

12:39.422 --> 12:40.465
No thanks.

12:41.049 --> 12:43.551
There's no way I can win against you.

12:44.177 --> 12:45.387
Tokio?

12:45.470 --> 12:48.348
Tokio has something
to discuss with me. Right?

12:52.310 --> 12:55.814
Fine then.
I guess I'll get Kona to play with me.

12:56.523 --> 12:58.817
[all gasp]

13:01.111 --> 13:04.030
Where on earth
does he get reflexes like that?

13:04.114 --> 13:05.156
Kona!

13:10.203 --> 13:13.289
[Mimihime] You said something about
the outside during the test, didn't you?

13:13.832 --> 13:16.042
[Tokio] Ah, no, that was…

13:18.086 --> 13:20.714
[Mimihime] What do you think
the outside is like, Tokio?

13:21.965 --> 13:22.966
Outside?

13:23.550 --> 13:26.428
Mmm… Why would you ask--

13:27.470 --> 13:30.557
Not here. Outside this wall.

13:30.640 --> 13:33.643
Huh? There's an outside beyond the wall?

13:34.144 --> 13:35.812
Isn't it just nothing?

13:35.895 --> 13:37.313
I think there is something else.

13:38.148 --> 13:40.734
I've always had a feeling that there is.

13:41.651 --> 13:44.738
And recently,
I've been able to imagine it more clearly.

13:46.489 --> 13:50.910
[Mimihime]
<i>When I think about wanting to go outside,</i>

13:50.994 --> 13:55.081
<i>two people from the outside come
to help me, and one of their faces…</i>

13:55.165 --> 13:56.332
DO YOU WANT TO GO OUTSIDE
OF THE OUTSIDE?

13:58.418 --> 14:00.086
<i>…is exactly the same as yours.</i>

14:04.674 --> 14:06.217
[footsteps]

14:08.344 --> 14:09.763
[Tokio] <i>Outside the room…</i>

14:11.306 --> 14:12.766
<i>outside the school…</i>

14:14.851 --> 14:16.227
<i>outside of…</i>

14:16.811 --> 14:17.854
<i>the outside.</i>

14:19.939 --> 14:21.149
[Director] Tokio?

14:22.817 --> 14:24.235
[Tokio] Director.

14:24.319 --> 14:27.405
If you can't sleep,
do you want some medicine?

14:27.489 --> 14:29.157
No, I…

14:30.742 --> 14:33.620
Is there an outside beyond this one?

14:33.703 --> 14:34.746
[gasps]

14:35.413 --> 14:38.041
Did you think of that yourself?

14:38.124 --> 14:39.292
[Tokio] Mimihime did.

14:39.793 --> 14:43.171
That girl has a sharp intuition.

14:43.254 --> 14:44.464
[aide] Director.

14:44.547 --> 14:47.801
[Director] It's only a matter of time
before they find out. Don't worry.

14:48.968 --> 14:50.053
Tokio?

14:52.222 --> 14:54.891
There is an outside beyond here.

14:57.018 --> 14:58.019
[Sis] Hey, Maru,

14:58.770 --> 15:02.774
it may surprise you to hear this,
coming from your bodyguard--

15:03.566 --> 15:06.611
[Maru] I'm pretty sure nothing you say
could surprise me anymore.

15:08.988 --> 15:10.573
I can't walk any further.

15:10.657 --> 15:11.825
What?

15:11.908 --> 15:14.786
[Sis] What? We've been sleeping outdoors,
traversing mountains.

15:14.869 --> 15:16.204
I've reached my limit.

15:16.996 --> 15:20.291
There's nothing to eat, nowhere to sleep.
I can't go on.

15:20.875 --> 15:25.839
All that talk of there being shops
on every corner before the Collapse…

15:25.922 --> 15:27.757
Was it all a lie?

15:27.841 --> 15:30.718
It's just because
we are on a path between cities.

15:30.802 --> 15:32.512
You're a city girl, aren't you?

15:32.595 --> 15:35.473
Exactly.
I'm a Tokyo girl through and through.

15:35.557 --> 15:36.850
-[thud]
-Ouch.

15:37.475 --> 15:39.686
Let's at least find
a decent spot to sleep.

15:40.186 --> 15:44.149
Where do you get so much energy from?
Is it because you're young?

15:44.232 --> 15:46.025
We're basically the same age.

15:46.609 --> 15:48.319
[Sis] You're 15, right?

15:48.403 --> 15:50.446
[Maru] I think so. You?

15:51.030 --> 15:54.450
[Sis] I'm 18, wait, 20.

15:54.534 --> 15:56.661
[Maru] What's with the two-year gap?

15:56.744 --> 15:58.746
[Sis] I'm not good with numbers, okay?

16:00.039 --> 16:01.457
[chickens clucking]

16:02.417 --> 16:04.210
[Sis] No way.

16:04.794 --> 16:06.212
[both gasp]

16:06.796 --> 16:08.673
That place is open?

16:09.257 --> 16:10.383
[inn owner] We are, yes.

16:12.552 --> 16:15.513
[inn owner] Nine, ten, eleven, twelve.

16:16.097 --> 16:17.390
All right, that'll do.

16:17.473 --> 16:20.560
Are you sure it's enough? It's so cheap.

16:21.269 --> 16:23.771
I feel bad. Take these too.

16:24.522 --> 16:26.649
Eh? Wow,

16:26.733 --> 16:29.569
AA batteries! Thank you!

16:30.153 --> 16:32.822
Can I look at the guest book?

16:32.906 --> 16:33.907
Go for it.

16:34.407 --> 16:37.368
You can't get batteries like this anymore!

16:37.452 --> 16:39.621
And in a place like this!

16:41.206 --> 16:42.290
He's not in here.

16:43.666 --> 16:46.252
Have you ever seen these two here?

16:46.336 --> 16:49.672
Ooh, he's good-looking.
If I had, I'd remember.

16:50.215 --> 16:51.299
What are their names?

16:51.799 --> 16:52.926
[Sis] Robin Inazaki.

16:53.426 --> 16:56.512
Well, I really don't know.

16:57.263 --> 16:59.307
What about the older, punky-looking one?

17:00.350 --> 17:02.977
I don't know his name.

17:03.561 --> 17:06.856
Everyone called him "Doc" or "Sir."

17:07.440 --> 17:08.650
[inn owner] I see.

17:09.150 --> 17:13.988
Oh, before I forget, have you ever heard
of a place called "Heaven"?

17:14.989 --> 17:16.199
Hmm…

17:16.741 --> 17:19.327
Well, that's how
everyone describes this place.

17:20.954 --> 17:23.498
It's heaven!

17:41.724 --> 17:42.976
-Kiruko.
-[gasps]

17:43.059 --> 17:45.186
[grunts] Eh, y-yes.

17:46.145 --> 17:48.398
The, uh, the mirror.

17:48.481 --> 17:52.068
That's a huge crack in the mirror!
I was just looking at it.

17:52.151 --> 17:53.152
Oh.

17:53.945 --> 17:57.532
The shower doesn't work,
but you can use the hot bath water.

17:58.366 --> 18:02.537
There are plenty of bottles,
but just use what you need.

18:02.620 --> 18:05.373
-The one that foams nicely is the shampoo.
-[Kiruko chuckles]

18:06.207 --> 18:08.042
[water running]

18:08.126 --> 18:09.294
[Kiruko] Eh?

18:14.299 --> 18:18.344
We don't have power reserves here,
you need to use that while the sun is up.

18:18.428 --> 18:19.512
Got it.

18:19.595 --> 18:21.264
[hair dryer blowing]

18:28.980 --> 18:29.981
Excuse me,

18:30.606 --> 18:33.526
that case, is it a gun case?

18:33.609 --> 18:37.280
Uh-huh. There's a monster
that prowls around this area.

18:38.114 --> 18:39.490
Don't go out wandering at night.

18:40.283 --> 18:41.909
-Monster…
-Hiruko.

18:41.993 --> 18:43.453
You mean a "Man-eater"?

18:45.371 --> 18:48.499
People call it different things,

18:48.583 --> 18:52.587
but it's this big, confusing shape,

18:52.670 --> 18:54.297
and it eats people.

18:55.798 --> 18:57.967
We can kill it.

19:00.928 --> 19:04.057
That's-- Guns have no effect on it.

19:04.140 --> 19:05.224
[Kiruko] We'll do it.

19:05.308 --> 19:07.894
My Kiru-Beam works on it, and this kid--

19:07.977 --> 19:08.978
Kiru-Beams?

19:09.062 --> 19:10.229
[Kiruko] What?

19:10.313 --> 19:11.606
[Maru] Kiru-Beam…

19:12.106 --> 19:14.734
Just because it's your beam,
you named it after yourself?

19:14.817 --> 19:16.986
[Kiruko] Why do you need the details?

19:17.528 --> 19:19.155
You already think it's weird anyway.

19:19.238 --> 19:21.491
[Maru] Exactly, it's weird.
That's why I'm asking.

19:25.536 --> 19:29.207
I've made a stew with some kind of
boar meat and vegetables, if you like?

19:29.707 --> 19:32.460
Really, we can have some?

19:37.090 --> 19:38.633
It's really good!

19:40.301 --> 19:43.096
I wanted to discuss
something with you both.

19:43.179 --> 19:45.181
Well, it's a bit tricky to find the words.

19:45.932 --> 19:50.728
Even though you two were raised
in these strange times,

19:50.812 --> 19:53.773
you use chopsticks perfectly,
and seem to have been educated well.

19:54.315 --> 19:57.068
I may be meddling,
but I have to say something.

19:58.444 --> 20:01.614
It's not my opinion,
or a rule or anything,

20:02.198 --> 20:04.617
but having children with a close relative,

20:05.660 --> 20:09.414
genetically speaking,
is fundamentally dangerous!

20:10.206 --> 20:12.208
What are you trying to say?

20:12.792 --> 20:17.004
-[Maru grunts]
-He might keep calling me "Sis,"

20:17.088 --> 20:19.257
but we are not even slightly related!

20:19.340 --> 20:23.010
And more to the point,
we are not even dating!

20:24.303 --> 20:25.304
Huh?

20:26.597 --> 20:29.016
I got completely the wrong idea!

20:29.100 --> 20:31.018
-Give me a break!
-[inn owner laughs]

20:31.102 --> 20:32.103
[sighs]

20:32.186 --> 20:34.939
I do all kinds of stuff in Tokyo,

20:35.022 --> 20:37.024
I'm sorta like an odd-job girl.

20:37.733 --> 20:40.778
I received a request to be
this guy's bodyguard during his travels.

20:41.779 --> 20:44.615
He is nothing to me
beyond an object of my protection.

20:50.705 --> 20:53.999
What's wrong, Maru?
Why are you suddenly so down?

20:54.917 --> 20:56.752
Why are you dragging your futon
so far away?

20:58.087 --> 21:01.007
-Hey, are you mad about something?
-[groans]

21:02.341 --> 21:04.760
[softly snoring]

21:05.887 --> 21:07.054
[Kiruko] Geez.

21:08.055 --> 21:10.016
So today you fall asleep straightaway…

21:11.726 --> 21:15.897
May as well go to sleep too then. [yawns]

21:16.647 --> 21:17.857
[stammers]

21:20.526 --> 21:21.527
Wow.

21:23.613 --> 21:25.364
Am I really that tired?

21:26.574 --> 21:27.700
Something…

21:28.576 --> 21:30.203
feels strange…

21:41.797 --> 21:44.217
[loading bullets]

22:03.444 --> 22:06.197
[Tokio]
<i>Is there an outside beyond this one?</i>

22:07.448 --> 22:09.617
There is an outside beyond here.

22:10.993 --> 22:15.831
However, it is a filthy world, a hell…

22:16.666 --> 22:18.292
[monster screeches]

22:18.376 --> 22:19.669
…where abhorrent monsters lurk.

22:20.711 --> 22:21.921
[screeching]

22:22.004 --> 22:23.923
HEAVEN AND HELL
